#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-setbuffer-to-data-arrays.md:1
msgid "SetBuffer for AOS and SOA Data Array Templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-setbuffer-to-data-arrays.md:3
msgid ""
"`vtkAOSDataArrayTemplate` and `vtkSOADataArrayTemplate` now provide a "
"`SetBuffer()` method that accepts a `vtkBuffer` (or `vtkAbstractBuffer` in "
"Python) to replace the array's internal storage. This enables zero-copy "
"buffer transfers between arrays without going through raw pointers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-setbuffer-to-data-arrays.md:8
msgid "AOS Arrays"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-setbuffer-to-data-arrays.md:10
msgid ""
"vtkNew<vtkBuffer<double>> buffer;\n"
"buffer->Allocate(100);\n"
"// ... fill buffer ...\n"
"\n"
"vtkNew<vtkDoubleArray> arr;\n"
"arr->SetNumberOfComponents(3);\n"
"arr->SetBuffer(buffer, true); // true = update MaxId from buffer size\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-setbuffer-to-data-arrays.md:20
msgid "SOA Arrays"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-setbuffer-to-data-arrays.md:22
msgid ""
"For SOA arrays, `SetBuffer()` takes a component index since each component "
"is stored separately:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-setbuffer-to-data-arrays.md:25
msgid ""
"vtkNew<vtkBuffer<double>> buf0;\n"
"buf0->Allocate(100);\n"
"\n"
"vtkNew<vtkSOADataArrayTemplate<double>> arr;\n"
"arr->SetNumberOfComponents(2);\n"
"arr->SetBuffer(0, buf0, true);  // set buffer for component 0\n"
"arr->SetBuffer(1, buf1, false); // set buffer for component 1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-setbuffer-to-data-arrays.md:35
msgid "Python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-setbuffer-to-data-arrays.md:37
msgid "`SetBuffer()` is fully wrapped for Python using `vtkAbstractBuffer`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-setbuffer-to-data-arrays.md:39
msgid ""
"src = vtkFloatArray()\n"
"src.SetNumberOfTuples(100)\n"
"\n"
"dst = vtkFloatArray()\n"
"dst.SetNumberOfComponents(1)\n"
"dst.SetBuffer(src.GetBuffer(), True)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-setbuffer-to-data-arrays.md:48
msgid "BufferChangedEvent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-setbuffer-to-data-arrays.md:50
msgid ""
"`SetBuffer()`, `SetArray()`, and `ShallowCopy()` now fire "
"`BufferChangedEvent` on both AOS and SOA array templates, matching the "
"existing behavior of `Resize()` and `InsertNextTuple()`. This ensures that "
"external consumers (such as NumPy views) are notified whenever the "
"underlying buffer changes."
msgstr ""
